{"event_categories":[{"category_id":"7b0adf61-0a93-4e3d-a7ef-1fee93c2591f","category_timing_id":1,"timing_id":17,"extra_timing_id":null,"sequence":16,"num_laps":17,"sprint_num_laps":null,"red_flag":13,"sprint_red_flag":null,"distance":{"meters":81617,"kiloMeters":81.62,"miles":50.71,"feet":267772.32}},{"category_id":"93888447-8746-4161-882c-e08a1d48447e","category_timing_id":3,"timing_id":17,"extra_timing_id":null,"sequence":16,"num_laps":24,"sprint_num_laps":12,"red_flag":18,"sprint_red_flag":9,"distance":{"meters":115224,"kiloMeters":115.22,"miles":71.6,"feet":378031.51}},{"category_id":"bc2b0143-1bfb-4ad0-9501-da2e474e3ea7","category_timing_id":2,"timing_id":17,"extra_timing_id":null,"sequence":16,"num_laps":19,"sprint_num_laps":null,"red_flag":14,"sprint_red_flag":null,"distance":{"meters":91219,"kiloMeters":91.22,"miles":56.68,"feet":299274.94}}],"country":"JP","circuit":{"id":"8bf0e0e7-6eb6-43b6-bab3-2aa21abad3ae","name":"Mobility Resort Motegi","iso_code":"JP","country":"Japan","region":"","city":"Motegi","postal_code":"321-3533","address":"Mobility Resort Motegi, 120-1 Hiyama, Motegi, Haga District, Tochigi 321-3533, Japan","lat":"36.531954","lng":"140.2253966","place_id":"ChIJI_AlOSvuIWARxAqhXAdR-b0","constructed":1997,"designer":"Twin Ring Motegi","modified":1997,"capacity":null,"active":true,"timing_id":76,"tracks":[{"id":"9fbd0109-0b0b-4bbb-a671-d7840036babe","first_grid":"2","box_entry":false,"box_exit":true,"lenght":"4801","lenght_units":{"meters":4801,"kiloMeters":4.8,"miles":2.98,"feet":15751.31},"width":"15","width_units":{"meters":15,"kiloMeters":0.02,"miles":0.01,"feet":49.21},"longest_straight":"762","longest_straight_units":{"meters":762,"kiloMeters":0.76,"miles":0.47,"feet":2500},"left_corners":"6","right_corners":"8","is_active":true,"timing_ids":[{"business_unit":"MGP","id":"76"},{"business_unit":"RKC","id":"76"},{"business_unit":"CEV","id":"76"},{"business_unit":"ATC","id":"76"}],"modification_date":"1999-04-23T00:00:00+00:00","assets":{"info":{"id":"45c998bf-d6ce-4581-889b-b8af6ecb69b4","name":"jpn-info.svg","type":"INFO","path":"https://photos.motogp.com/events-admin/9/f/9fbd0109-0b0b-4bbb-a671-d7840036babe/info/jpn-info.svg","mimetype":"SVG"},"simple":{"id":"fa41fa20-7e1c-4e97-a6c9-79055f7d4172","name":"jpn.png","type":"SIMPLE","path":"https://photos.motogp.com/events-admin/9/f/9fbd0109-0b0b-4bbb-a671-d7840036babe/simple/jpn.png","mimetype":"PNG"}}},{"id":"ef5090d2-187c-4d58-a799-08b9c94cbaf9","first_grid":"2","box_entry":false,"box_exit":true,"lenght":"1490","lenght_units":{"meters":1490,"kiloMeters":1.49,"miles":0.93,"feet":4888.45},"width":"15","width_units":{"meters":15,"kiloMeters":0.02,"miles":0.01,"feet":49.21},"longest_straight":"762","longest_straight_units":{"meters":762,"kiloMeters":0.76,"miles":0.47,"feet":2500},"left_corners":"3","right_corners":"","is_active":false,"timing_ids":[{"business_unit":"MGP","id":"68"},{"business_unit":"RKC","id":"68"},{"business_unit":"CEV","id":"68"},{"business_unit":"ATC","id":"68"}],"modification_date":"1999-04-23T00:00:00+00:00","assets":[]}],"circuit_descriptions":[{"id":"1ce5889d-5b3f-444b-942b-b7eb1273445a","business_unit_id":{"id":"d6ced16c-c25e-4f61-bfa5-4683679ff873"},"business_unit_name":{"value":"MotoGP™"},"language":"de","description":"Die Doppelring-Rennbahn Motegi in Japan liegt in der schönen Natur des Nord-Kanto Bezirks. Die Rennstrecke besteht aus einem 2,4 km langen Oval und einem vier Kilometer langen Straßenkurs, der nach den internationalen Standards entworfen wurde. Honda entwarf die Strecke im August 1997 als ultimative Testfahrbahn. Im Jahr 2000 ist die Strecke Zuhause des MotoGP geworden, während die ovale Strecke entworfen wurde, um die amerikanische Rennsportkultur ins Land zu bringen.</p>\n\n<p>Die Doppelbahn Motegi ist eine ganzjährige Attraktion für Fans, da sie auch Schauplatz der Honda Collection Hall ist, einem Museum, das eine berühmte Sammlung von Motorrädern, Autos und Rennmaschinen aus verschiedenen Zeiten zeigt. Der Komplex umfasst ebenso eine Sicherheits- und Rennschule, Dirt Track, Go Karts, Hotel, Restaurant, Geschäfte und Event-Hallen. Derzeit sind dort rund 300 Mitarbeiter beschäftigt."},{"id":"20718237-3e02-403c-b377-05aced11fbd5","business_unit_id":{"id":"d6ced16c-c25e-4f61-bfa5-4683679ff873"},"business_unit_name":{"value":"MotoGP™"},"language":"fr","description":"Situé dans le Kanto, le Twin Ring Motegi doit son nom aux deux tracés distincts qu’il propose : un ovale de 2,4 km et un circuit routier de 4,6 km. Commandité par Honda en 1997 en tant que base d’essais, le circuit routier accueille le Championnat du Monde MotoGP depuis 1999. Le Twin Ring Motegi attire les amateurs de sports mécaniques tout au long de l’année grâce au musée Honda où sont exposées de nombreuses machines, motos et voitures, qui ont marqué l’histoire du constructeur japonais. Le complexe abrite aussi une école de pilotage, des pistes tout-terrain et de kart, ainsi que divers commerces."},{"id":"6754dabd-5974-4f90-b3b9-89dde5c397c2","business_unit_id":{"id":"d6ced16c-c25e-4f61-bfa5-4683679ff873"},"business_unit_name":{"value":"MotoGP™"},"language":"it","description":"Situato su un posto montano di grande bellezza, nel distretto di Kanto, il circuito giapponese di Twin Ring Motegi possiede un ovale di 2,5 km e una pista classica di una lunghezza di 4,8 km disegnata secondo le norme internazionali. Costruito dalla Honda come laboratorio di prove delle loro differenti produzioni nell'agosto 1997, il circuito di Twin Ring è diventato dal 1999 lo scenario di un Gran Premio del Campionato del Mondo, mentre il tracciato ovale ha permesso di introdurre nel paese le competizioni automobilistiche di ispirazione americana.</p>\n\n<p>Il circuito di Motegi attrae durante l'anno gli amanti del motore, dato che il suo gigantesco recinto ospita il Museo Honda, che esibisce in maniera permanente moto e automobili da competizione di tutte le epoche. Inoltre, questo complesso sportivo si completa con una scuola guida, piste di dirt-trarck e go-kart, hotel, ristorante, negozi e altri servizi che impiegano attualmente 300 persone."},{"id":"74464c61-89a9-49dd-b46d-b8c28cb1fd6d","business_unit_id":{"id":"d6ced16c-c25e-4f61-bfa5-4683679ff873"},"business_unit_name":{"value":"MotoGP™"},"language":"en","description":"Located amongst the vast natural beauty of the northern Kanto district, the twin ring circuit at Motegi in Japan consists of a 1.5 mile oval and a 2.9 mile road course constructed to international standards. Built by Honda as the ultimate test facility in August 1997, the road circuit became home to MotoGP in 1999 whilst the oval is designed to introduce American motorsports culture to the country."},{"id":"afaefd28-d341-4917-87ce-827d91f138db","business_unit_id":{"id":"d6ced16c-c25e-4f61-bfa5-4683679ff873"},"business_unit_name":{"value":"MotoGP™"},"language":"ja","description":"<p>栃木県の緑豊かな茂木町で１９９７年８月に開業したツインリンクもてぎは、英語のツインとドイツ語のリンクをつなぎ合わせた造語で、アメリカンスタイルのオーバルコース、ヨーロッパスタイルのロードコースの２つのレーシングコースを表すと共に、人と自然の触れ合いや調和、人と人との出会いや結び付きの意味を込めて名づけられた。</p>\n<p>開業から１年半後の１９９９年４月に日本ＧＰを初開催。当時は鈴鹿サーキットと隔年開催となる予定だったが、初開催時の実績が評価され、２０００年から４月に鈴鹿サーキットで日本ＧＰ、１０月にツインリンクもてぎでパシフィックＧＰを開催。</p>\n<p>２００４年から２００８年まで毎年９月に日本ＧＰを開催した後、２００９年から４月開催を計画していたが、２０１０年はアイスランドの火山噴火により、欧州で大規模な空路封鎖が発生したことから１０月に延期。２０１１年は東日本大震災により、１ヶ月ほどの営業休止を強いられたため１０月に延期。２０１２年以降は秋に開催。</p>\n<p>２００６年、本田技研工業の１００％子会社から、鈴鹿サーキットを運営する鈴鹿サーキットランドと対等合併し、モビリティランドとして新たにスタートすると、２０１２年３月にはドルナスポーツとの間で、２０１４年から５年間の開催に関して合意。開業２０周年を迎えた２０１７年８月には、２０１９年から５年間の延長開催に関して合意し、２０２３年までの開催が決定。</p>\n<p>２２年連続の開催を予定していた２０２０年と翌年の２０２１年は、新型コロナウイルスの影響を受けて開催が見送れたことから、２０２３年までの契約期間を２０２５年まで延長すると、２０２５年７月に２０２６年から５年間の開催に関して契約を更新。\n<p>２０２１年１０月、２０２２年３月１日付で社名を『株式会社モビリティランド』から『ホンダモビリティランド株式会社』、開場２５周年を迎える『ツインリンクもてぎ』を『モビリティリゾートもてぎ』に変更。</p>\n<p>通算２６回目の開催となる２０２６年は、シーズン１６戦目として１０月２日から４日に催行。</p>\n"},{"id":"bcf7689e-28c0-4113-af0f-56f2ae7e3a1b","business_unit_id":{"id":"d6ced16c-c25e-4f61-bfa5-4683679ff873"},"business_unit_name":{"value":"MotoGP™"},"language":"pt","description":"Cercado pela beleza natural da região norte de Kanto, no Japão, o circuito de Motegi é um complexo singular no calendário. Conhecido como Twin Ring Motegi, ele reúne dois traçados distintos: um oval de 1,5 milha e um circuito misto de 2,9 milhas, ambos construídos dentro dos mais altos padrões internacionais.\n\nInaugurado em agosto de 1997 e desenvolvido pela Honda como um centro de testes de referência mundial, Motegi rapidamente ganhou protagonismo. O circuito misto passou a receber a MotoGP a partir de 1999, tornando-se a casa do GP do Japão, enquanto o oval foi projetado com a proposta de aproximar o público japonês da cultura do automobilismo norte-americano.\n\nÉ uma pista que valoriza aceleração forte e frenagens intensas, especialmente nas zonas de stop and go, exigindo precisão milimétrica dos pilotos. Em Motegi, técnica e potência caminham juntas, num cenário que mistura tradição, tecnologia e a paixão japonesa pelo detalhe."},{"id":"eafeb1e5-7854-4927-b67f-6f16825d4cbf","business_unit_id":{"id":"d6ced16c-c25e-4f61-bfa5-4683679ff873"},"business_unit_name":{"value":"MotoGP™"},"language":"es","description":"Enclavado en un paraje montañoso de gran belleza, en el distrito de Kanto, el circuito japonés de Twin Ring Motegi posee un óvalo de 2,5 kms. y una pista clásica de una longitud de 4,8 kms diseñada según las normas internacionales. Construido por Honda como laboratorio de pruebas de sus diferentes producciones en agosto de 1997, el circuito Twin Ring se ha convertido desde 1999 en escenario de un Gran Premio del Campeonato del Mundo, mientras que el trazado oval ha permitido introducir en el país las competiciones automovilísticas de inspiración norteamericana.</p>  \n<p>El circuito de Motegi atrae a lo largo del año a los amantes del motor, ya que su gigantesco recinto alberga el Museo Honda, que exhibe con carácter permanente motos y coches de competición de todas las épocas. Además, este complejo deportivo se completa con una escuela de pilotaje, pistas de dirt-track y go-kart, hotel, restaurante, tiendas y otros servicios que emplean actualmente a 300 personas. "}],"user_location":{"lat":"36.532963","lng":"140.226759","radius":2500},"track":{"id":"9fbd0109-0b0b-4bbb-a671-d7840036babe","first_grid":"2","box_entry":false,"box_exit":true,"lenght":"4801","lenght_units":{"meters":4801,"kiloMeters":4.8,"miles":2.98,"feet":15751.31},"width":"15","width_units":{"meters":15,"kiloMeters":0.02,"miles":0.01,"feet":49.21},"longest_straight":"762","longest_straight_units":{"meters":762,"kiloMeters":0.76,"miles":0.47,"feet":2500},"left_corners":"6","right_corners":"8","is_active":true,"timing_ids":[{"business_unit":"MGP","id":"76"},{"business_unit":"RKC","id":"76"},{"business_unit":"CEV","id":"76"},{"business_unit":"ATC","id":"76"}],"modification_date":"1999-04-23T00:00:00+00:00","assets":{"info":{"id":"45c998bf-d6ce-4581-889b-b8af6ecb69b4","name":"jpn-info.svg","type":"INFO","path":"https://photos.motogp.com/events-admin/9/f/9fbd0109-0b0b-4bbb-a671-d7840036babe/info/jpn-info.svg","mimetype":"SVG"},"simple":{"id":"fa41fa20-7e1c-4e97-a6c9-79055f7d4172","name":"jpn.png","type":"SIMPLE","path":"https://photos.motogp.com/events-admin/9/f/9fbd0109-0b0b-4bbb-a671-d7840036babe/simple/jpn.png","mimetype":"PNG"}}}},"type":"SPORT","urls":[{"id":"040bc198-4eaf-4420-a390-45c04c215dec","language":"pt","url":"https://motogppremier.motogp.com/2026-motogp-japan?package-group=fan&utm_source=motogp.com&utm_medium=partner_referral&utm_campaign=motogp_web_japan_exp","type":"PREMIER"},{"id":"107024d4-6afb-4b8f-ab2a-0d75c0757efc","language":"de","url":"https://motogppremier.motogp.com/2026-motogp-japan?package-group=hospitality&utm_source=motogp.com&utm_medium=partner_referral&utm_campaign=motogp_web_japan_hosp","type":"HOSPITALITY"},{"id":"1ffd85d9-c6ff-4abe-8602-f7923dbba16e","language":"en","url":"https://tickets.motogp.com/en/21091-japan/tickets/?utm_source=motogp.com&utm_medium=web&utm_campaign=calendar_jpn_en","type":"TICKETING"},{"id":"27881c51-9540-4cb5-bcd2-a108a5